Time Complexity:

Let n = size of array

    Single traversal of array → O(n)

Overall: O(n)


Space Complexity: O(1)


Approach:

1. Traverse the array from index 0 to n-2
2. Compare current element with next element
3. If arr[i+1] < arr[i], array is not sorted → return false
4. If no such violation is found, array is sorted
5. Return true





class Solution {
    public boolean isSorted(int[] arr) {
        // code here
        for(int i=0; i<arr.length-1; i++){
            if(arr[i+1]<arr[i]) return false;
        }
        return true;
    }
}
